title: "Clinical Verifiable Gates (CVG)"
version: "0.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21328660"
authors:
  - given-names: "Sergey"
    family-names: "Morev"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sergey-morev/clinical-verifiable-gates"
url: "https://github.com/sergey-morev/clinical-verifiable-gates"
abstract: >-
  Clinical Verifiable Gates (CVG) is an open-source reference
  implementation of deterministic runtime qualification gates for bounded,
  safety-sensitive clinical AI outputs. Version 0.1.0 provides
  schema-validated PASS, BLOCK, and ABSTAIN adjudication, deterministic
  evidence grounding and polarity-conflict containment, an evaluation-only
  Silence oracle, approved machine-readable fixtures, a canonical reviewer
  demo, regression tests, and Python 3.11 continuous integration. CVG is
  research and engineering tooling only; it is not a medical device, a
  clinically validated diagnostic system, a model extractor, or
  deployment-ready clinical software.
keywords:
  - "clinical artificial intelligence"
  - "deterministic verification"
  - "runtime gating"
  - "evidence grounding"
  - "abstention"
  - "research software"
